 "geometry": {
  "width": 9,
  "height": 5,
  "depth": 6,
  "apron_rows": 3,
  "apron_margin": 1,
  "ramp_max": 14,
  "backing": 2,
  "clear_above": 2,
  "max_fill": 3,
  "max_cut": 14,
  "rules": "A face is a box `width` along the face, `depth` into the rock and `height` high, worked from its `front` (north: the front plane is the box's z0 and the rock runs +z; south z1, -z; west x0, +x; east x1, -x; along the face u runs +x on a north or south face, +z on a west or east face). The cut: row r in front of the front plane (r = 1, 2, ...) spans u = -apron_margin .. width - 1 + apron_margin. Its floor t starts at the box's y0 - 1; rows 1..apron_rows keep it; from row apron_rows + 1 on, a row whose every column's ground is within 1 of t ends the cut (it is not written), else t moves one toward the row's median ground (the lower median of the sorted columns) and the row is written; a cut longer than apron_rows + ramp_max rows is refused. A written column: host rock from ground + 1 to t - 1 (a built-up column), the floor block at t, and air from t + 1 to max(ground, t) + clear_above (and at least to the box top + 1 in the apron rows); no column dug more than max_cut or built up more than max_fill. The skin: every cell next to the cut's air (four sides and below), not otherwise written and at or under its column's ground, becomes host rock. The backing: host rock in every cell of u = -backing .. width - 1 + backing, d = 0 .. depth - 1 + backing, y = y0 - backing .. y1 + backing outside the box. The bedrock (only where the site says): the shell one further out, d from 1, never on the front plane. The ore of variant k: n = ore_min + h32(seed, face, k) mod (ore_max - ore_min + 1) cells, in the order h32(seed, face, k, x, y, z) sorts them: first visible_min on the front plane's bottom row with 1 <= u <= width - 2, then the rest at depth 2 or more under the top row (tools/mines.py ore_cells)."
 },
