  "why": "STONE_ECONOMY.md 5.3 and 6.2: at least 600 s (12,000 ticks) between restores of a face, checked only on approach (fill fails on an unloaded chunk, so a fixed timer would mostly fail silently): every 100 ticks, only while a player is inside the site's approach box (the faces' bounds grown by approach_margin across, approach_down below and approach_up above); the two faces of one stone at a place kept 300 s (6,000 ticks) apart. Game time and the scores are saved with the world, so a restart neither repeats nor loses a restore",
